1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,920
Pipe Up is a backup channel for people who
stutter, in Google Meet.

2
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:14,463
In a video call, a block can look like a
frozen connection.

3
00:00:14,543 --> 00:00:18,920
People talk over you, and the moment is
gone.

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,520
Pipe Up gives you one key to hold the
floor,

5
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,320
and short replies from your own notes.

6
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,720
Firebase AI Logic runs them on Gemini
Nano, on your device.

7
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,920
The cloud is used only if you agree.

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,990
This scene is staged. Sam is in a block.

9
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:41,490
[Colleague] Sam, are you frozen?

10
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:46,457
Sam presses Alt+1. Everyone sees his
message in the chat.

11
00:00:46,537 --> 00:00:51,920
He finishes his sentence himself, then
presses 4: I answered myself.

12
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:58,252
Before the call, Sam writes his positions
and notes, or adds a document.

13
00:00:58,332 --> 00:01:02,220
Prepare for the call turns them into
likely questions,

14
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,865
with short answers he can edit.

15
00:01:04,945 --> 00:01:08,393
The cloud does this once, after he
confirms.

16
00:01:08,473 --> 00:01:11,920
During the call, the device does the rest.

17
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,112
A question about the deadline.

18
00:01:15,192 --> 00:01:18,740
After the pause, three short replies
appear.

19
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:24,442
This one comes from Sam's briefing. The
badge says On device.

20
00:01:24,522 --> 00:01:29,108
Nothing is sent until Sam presses 1, then
Enter.

21
00:01:29,188 --> 00:01:34,291
The log shows where each reply was
generated, and why.

22
00:01:34,371 --> 00:01:37,920
It reads inferenceSource from Firebase AI
Logic.

23
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:43,073
On a computer without Gemini Nano, Pipe Up
asks first.

24
00:01:43,153 --> 00:01:49,903
If Sam agrees, only the last two caption
lines go to Gemini in the cloud,

25
00:01:49,983 --> 00:01:51,724
protected by App Check.

26
00:01:51,804 --> 00:01:54,456
His briefing needs a second opt-in.

27
00:01:54,536 --> 00:01:57,643
His past replies never leave the device.

28
00:01:57,723 --> 00:01:59,920
Now the badge says Cloud.

29
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,892
Sam can also have a reply read aloud in
the call.

30
00:02:04,972 --> 00:02:07,675
The voice is made on his computer.

31
00:02:07,755 --> 00:02:12,842
It is clearly synthetic, and it is not a
copy of his voice.

32
00:02:12,922 --> 00:02:16,342
[Synthetic voice reads the reply]

33
00:02:16,422 --> 00:02:19,920
With Alt+D, he tells colleagues in his own
words.

34
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,120
Reading under pressure is hard.

35
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:28,320
So there is easy reading, one suggestion
at a time,

36
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,920
high contrast and reduced motion.

37
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,032
Pipe Up has no stealth mode.

38
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:39,476
What it sends is visible or audible to
everyone, as coming from Sam.

39
00:02:39,556 --> 00:02:43,664
It has not yet been tested with people who
stutter.

40
00:02:43,744 --> 00:02:44,920
That comes next.

41
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:49,920
Pipe Up. Your voice first, and a backup
when you need it.
